---
description: Avoid duplicate controls that perform the same local action
alwaysApply: true
---

# One outcome, one control

Do not render multiple nearby interactive controls that produce the same outcome.

- If a row, card, image, label, or field is already tappable, do not add a separate icon or button that repeats its action.
- Prefer one accessible hit target around the meaningful content when the whole region has one action.
- Editable inputs do not need an adjacent edit/focus button.
- Keep a second control only when it performs a distinct action. A non-interactive chevron or status icon may communicate affordance without becoming another control.
- Give the surviving control one accurate accessibility label and one stable `ontrack.*` testID.

When touching a screen, scan the local section for repeated handlers, duplicated accessibility labels, and action copy that describes an already-adjacent button. Consolidate confirmed duplicates without removing distinct destructive, cancel, navigation, or secondary actions.
